LIB_LOAD("pg",{"pg1":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where was Nicolas Herman born?","o":["Lorraine","Lagos","London","Rome"],"why":"Around 1614."},{"q":"What did a bare winter tree show Nicolas?","o":["God's providence and power","That winter is boring","That trees die","Nothing"],"why":"Spring would come again."},{"q":"\"He shall be like a ___ planted by the rivers of water.\"","o":["tree","rock","house","ship"],"why":"Psalm 1:3."},{"q":"What happened to Nicolas as a soldier?","o":["He was wounded and limped for life","He became a general","He never fought","He became rich"],"why":"Then he became a footman."},{"q":"What did Nicolas break as a footman?","o":["Everything!","Nothing","Only the door","Only his shoes"],"why":"A great awkward fellow."},{"q":"\"My strength is made perfect in...\"","o":["weakness","money","speed","pride"],"why":"2 Corinthians 12:9."},{"q":"What name was Nicolas given in the monastery?","o":["Brother Lawrence","Brother John","Father Paul","Saint Nicolas"],"why":"In 1640."},{"q":"What does Jesus give the heavy laden?","o":["Rest","More work","A crown","Gold"],"why":"Matthew 11:28."},{"q":"Who recorded Brother Lawrence's conversations?","o":["Joseph de Beaufort","John Bunyan","E. M. Bounds","Andrew Murray"],"why":"And gathered his letters."},{"q":"What is the name of Brother Lawrence's famous book?","o":["The Practice of the Presence of God","The Pilgrim's Progress","The Holy War","Quo Vadis"],"why":"Still read worldwide."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What job did Brother Lawrence do in the monastery?","o":["He was the cook","He was the head monk","He was a soldier","He was a banker"],"why":"Coming up in Chapter 2!"},"choices":[{"title":"Feeling empty","q":"You feel low, like nothing good is happening in your life.","o":[{"t":"Remember the bare tree: tell God how you feel and trust Him to bring new life.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Winter isn't the end. God brings spring."},{"t":"Decide things will never change.","f":"A bare tree in winter isn't dead."},{"t":"Keep it all to yourself.","f":"Talk to God, and to a trusted adult too."}]},{"title":"Clumsy day","q":"You knocked over a classmate's project by accident and everyone laughed. You feel useless.","o":[{"t":"Apologise, help fix it, and remember God uses clumsy people too.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God called a footman who broke everything."},{"t":"Decide you're useless.","f":"God's strength works through weakness."},{"t":"Blame someone else.","f":"Own it, help fix it, and move on."}]},{"title":"Not good enough","q":"After a bad week, you think God couldn't possibly accept you.","o":[{"t":"Come to Jesus honestly and rest in His love.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Come unto me, and I will give you rest."},{"t":"Try to be perfect first, then come to God.","f":"You can't earn His love. Just come."},{"t":"Avoid God until you feel better.","f":"That's when you need Him most."}]},{"title":"The quiet one","q":"There's an old lady at church who always seems peaceful. You've never spoken to her.","o":[{"t":"Go and ask her how she stays close to God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like de Beaufort, learn from quiet, faithful people."},{"t":"Ignore her. She's old.","f":"Quiet people often have the deepest wisdom."},{"t":"Talk about her behind her back.","f":"Get to know her instead."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"wintertree","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of The Practice of the Presence of God in real life."},{"sc":"wintertree","n":"🌳 Winter isn't the end. God brings new life."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"💥 God calls clumsy, ordinary people too."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"⛪ Come to Jesus and rest. You can't earn His love."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"📖 God notices quiet faithfulness."}],"stops":{"pg1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","n":"Around 1614, in a small village in {Lorraine}, a boy called Nicolas Herman was born. His family were poor, ordinary country people."},{"sc":"wintertree","n":"When Nicolas was about eighteen, he was walking one winter day when he stopped in front of a tree. It was completely bare. No leaves. No flowers. No fruit. It looked dead."},{"sc":"wintertree","w":"nicolas","e":"worried","t":"Look at it. Grey and empty. Nothing at all."},{"sc":"wintertree","w":"nicolas","e":"smile","t":"But wait... in a few months, spring will come. New leaves will burst out. Then flowers. Then fruit. Who does that? Only God."},{"sc":"wintertree","n":"In that moment, Nicolas saw how great and caring God is. If God could bring a dead-looking tree back to life every spring, He could look after Nicolas too."},{"sc":"wintertree","n":"He later told a friend that this one moment set his heart free from loving the world, and lit a love for God in him that never went out, for the rest of his long life."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"worried","t":"Sometimes I feel like that bare tree. Like nothing good is growing in me."},{"sc":"wintertree","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Then remember my tree, child. Winter isn't the end. The same God who brings spring to the trees can bring new life to you."}],"quote":{"text":"Seeing a tree stripped of its leaves, and considering that within a little time the leaves would be renewed, and after that the flowers and fruit appear, he received a high view of the providence and power of God.","who":"Joseph de Beaufort, The First Conversation","tag":"From the Conversations"},"lesson":{"title":"Winter isn't the end","text":"A bare winter tree showed young Nicolas how great and caring God is: He brings dead-looking trees back to life every spring. That sight lit a love for God that lasted all his life. If you feel bare and empty, God can bring spring to you too."},"think":"What does a tree coming back to life in spring tell you about God? Where in your life do you need God's 'spring'?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Brother Lawrence's name before he became a monk?","o":["Nicolas Herman","John Ploughman","Joseph Beaufort","Andrew Murray"],"why":"Born around 1614 in Lorraine."},{"q":"What did Nicolas see in winter that changed his life?","o":["A bare tree","A snowman","A river","A church"],"why":"No leaves, no flowers, no fruit."},{"q":"About how old was he?","o":["Eighteen","Five","Forty","Eighty"],"why":"A young man."},{"q":"What did he think about the tree?","o":["That God would bring it back to life in spring","That it was dead forever","That it should be cut down","Nothing"],"why":"He saw God's providence and power."},{"q":"What did that moment light in his heart?","o":["A love for God that never went out","A fear of winter","A love of trees only","Nothing"],"why":"For the rest of his life."}]},"pg1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"battle","n":"Nicolas grew up in a time of terrible wars. As a young man, he became a soldier."},{"sc":"battle","w":"pgsoldier","e":"worried","t":"War is nothing like the stories. It's frightening and cruel."},{"sc":"battle","n":"He was badly wounded in the leg. For the rest of his life, he walked with a limp."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"After the army, he got a job as a {footman} in the house of a rich man in Paris. But it didn't go well."},{"sc":"mansion","w":"lawrence","e":"smirk","t":"I'll be honest with you. I was a great awkward fellow who broke everything! Plates, cups, you name it. Crash!"},{"sc":"mansion","w":"pgikenna","e":"big","t":"Ha! That sounds like me. I dropped my mum's best bowl last week."},{"sc":"mansion","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Then we have something in common! But here's the wonderful thing: God doesn't only call the clever, graceful, talented people. He called a clumsy, limping footman. And He calls you."},{"sc":"mansion","n":"Paul wrote that God's strength works best through our weakness. Nicolas was about to find out how true that is."}],"quote":{"text":"He had been footman to M. Fieubert, the treasurer, and was a great awkward fellow who broke everything.","who":"Joseph de Beaufort, The First Conversation","tag":"From the Conversations"},"lesson":{"title":"God calls the clumsy too","text":"Nicolas was a wounded soldier and a footman who broke everything. He wasn't graceful or impressive. But God called him anyway, and his life still helps millions. God's strength works best through our weakness."},"think":"What weakness or clumsiness do you worry about? How might God use you anyway?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Nicolas become as a young man?","o":["A soldier","A king","A sailor","A teacher"],"why":"In a time of terrible wars."},{"q":"What happened to his leg?","o":["He was badly wounded and limped for life","He broke it climbing","Nothing","He lost it"],"why":"He walked with a limp ever after."},{"q":"What job did he have in Paris after the army?","o":["A footman","A cook","A banker","A farmer"],"why":"In a rich man's house."},{"q":"How did he describe himself as a footman?","o":["A great awkward fellow who broke everything","The best servant ever","A rich man","Very graceful"],"why":"Crash!"},{"q":"According to 2 Corinthians 12:9, where is God's strength made perfect?","o":["In weakness","In strength","In money","In fame"],"why":"My grace is sufficient for thee."}]},"pg1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"In 1640, Nicolas joined the {Carmelites}, a community of monks in Paris devoted to prayer. He became a {lay brother} and was given a new name: Brother Lawrence."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"You might think he was happy straight away. But for about ten years he struggled. He worried that he wasn't good enough for God, and that God might not accept him."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"worried","t":"I kept thinking about my sins. I felt sure I'd never be good enough. I was anxious and troubled for a long time."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"But Jesus had already spoken words for people exactly like Brother Lawrence."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"pgjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"Slowly, Brother Lawrence stopped trying to earn God's love, and simply trusted Him. Peace came, deep peace. And it never left him."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"I gave up trying to be good enough on my own, and gave myself completely to God. Since then, I've known His peace."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"smile","t":"So even a monk felt 'not good enough' sometimes. And Jesus' answer was: come to Me, and rest."}],"quote":{"text":"Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls.","who":"Matthew 11:29","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Come and rest","text":"For about ten years, Brother Lawrence worried he wasn't good enough for God. Peace came when he stopped trying to earn God's love and simply trusted Him. Jesus says to everyone who's tired and anxious: come to Me, and I will give you rest."},"think":"Do you ever feel 'not good enough' for God? What would it look like to come to Jesus and rest?","quiz":[{"q":"In what year did Nicolas join the monastery?","o":["1640","1840","1440","1940"],"why":"In Paris."},{"q":"What new name was he given?","o":["Brother Lawrence","Brother Nicolas","Father Joseph","Saint Paul"],"why":"As a lay brother."},{"q":"What did he struggle with for about ten years?","o":["Worrying he wasn't good enough for God","Cooking","Learning to read","Being too rich"],"why":"He was anxious and troubled."},{"q":"What does Jesus promise those who come to Him?","o":["Rest","Riches","More work","Fame"],"why":"Matthew 11:28."},{"q":"How did peace finally come?","o":["He stopped trying to earn God's love and trusted Him","He worked harder","He left the monastery","He forgot about God"],"why":"And it never left him."}]},"pg1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"Brother Lawrence never planned to write a famous book. He was just a cook. But people began to notice something different about him: a deep, quiet joy."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"A church leader called {Joseph de Beaufort} heard about him and came to visit. They sat and talked about God."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"beaufort","e":"smile","t":"Brother Lawrence, how is it that you seem so close to God all the time, even in that busy kitchen?"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"It is very simple, Father. I just talk with Him, all day long, whatever I'm doing."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"De Beaufort wrote down their conversations. Brother Lawrence also wrote letters to friends who asked for help. After he died, these were gathered into a little book: The Practice of the Presence of God."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"More than three hundred years later, people all over the world, in many languages, still read it."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgikenna","e":"smile","t":"A cook's conversations ended up as a book read all over the world? That's amazing!"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"beaufort","e":"big","t":"God notices the quiet people who love Him. And sometimes, He lets the whole world notice them too."}],"quote":{"text":"Then they that feared the LORD spake often one to another: and the LORD hearkened, and heard it, and a book of remembrance was written before him.","who":"Malachi 3:16","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God notices quiet faithfulness","text":"Brother Lawrence was a quiet kitchen monk, but his deep joy got noticed. Joseph de Beaufort wrote down their conversations, and after he died, they became a book still read worldwide. God sees quiet faithfulness, and remembers it."},"think":"Who is a quiet person in your life who loves God deeply? What could you learn by talking with them?","quiz":[{"q":"What did people notice about Brother Lawrence?","o":["A deep, quiet joy","His fame","His riches","His loud voice"],"why":"So de Beaufort came to visit."},{"q":"Who wrote down their conversations?","o":["Joseph de Beaufort","Brother Lawrence's mother","A king","Nicolas the soldier"],"why":"A French church leader."},{"q":"How did Brother Lawrence say he stayed close to God?","o":["By talking with Him all day long","By leaving the kitchen","By never working","By shouting"],"why":"Whatever he was doing."},{"q":"When was the book gathered together?","o":["After he died","When he was a boy","Before he joined the monastery","Last year"],"why":"From conversations and letters."},{"q":"According to Malachi 3:16, what did the LORD do when His people spoke together?","o":["He hearkened and heard it","He ignored them","He slept","He was angry"],"why":"A book of remembrance was written."}]}}},"pg2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What job did Brother Lawrence do in the monastery?","o":["Cook","Banker","Soldier","Farmer"],"why":"For about fifteen years."},{"q":"What does 'aversion' mean?","o":["A strong dislike","A great love","A song","A recipe"],"why":"He disliked kitchen work."},{"q":"Colossians 3:17: whatsoever ye do, do all in the name of...?","o":["the Lord Jesus","your teacher","the king","yourself"],"why":"Giving thanks."},{"q":"Who sat at Jesus' feet?","o":["Mary","Martha","Peter","Bisola"],"why":"She chose the good part."},{"q":"\"But one thing is...\"","o":["needful","boring","difficult","finished"],"why":"Luke 10:42."},{"q":"What was Brother Lawrence's Martha-and-Mary secret?","o":["Busy hands, listening heart","Never cook","Never pray","Cook only on Sundays"],"why":"Martha with his hands, Mary with his heart."},{"q":"What does God look at in our work?","o":["The love behind it","Its size","Its price","Who sees it"],"why":"Little things, great love."},{"q":"\"Whatsoever ye do, do all to the ___ of God.\"","o":["glory","fear","house","book"],"why":"1 Corinthians 10:31."},{"q":"How did Brother Lawrence get around the boat?","o":["He rolled over the barrels","He jumped","He was carried","He used a rope"],"why":"In Burgundy!"},{"q":"Philippians 4:6: be careful for...?","o":["nothing","everything","money","tomorrow"],"why":"Pray instead."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'tranquillity' mean?","o":["Calm, peaceful quiet","Loud noise","Great speed","A kind of food"],"why":"Lawrence had God in tranquillity, even in the kitchen."},"choices":[{"title":"Dish duty","q":"It's your turn to wash the dishes and you're in a bad mood about it.","o":[{"t":"Do it for God: thank Him and pray for your family as you wash.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! The sink can be a holy place."},{"t":"Do it badly so you're not asked again.","f":"Small things, done with love, matter to God."},{"t":"Complain the whole time.","f":"Try talking to God instead."}]},{"title":"Too busy for God","q":"Exam week. You're so busy you've forgotten God completely.","o":[{"t":"Keep studying, but talk to God as you go: before, during and after.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Martha with your hands, Mary with your heart."},{"t":"Leave God until exams are over.","f":"One thing is needful, especially in busy times."},{"t":"Stop studying and only pray.","f":"Do both: busy hands, listening heart."}]},{"title":"Nobody notices","q":"You tidy the classroom every day and nobody ever says thank you.","o":[{"t":"Keep doing it for the love of God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God sees the love behind the smallest jobs."},{"t":"Stop, since nobody cares.","f":"God cares."},{"t":"Remind everyone how much you do.","f":"Do it for God, not for praise."}]},{"title":"Out of your depth","q":"You've been chosen to lead a group project, but you're not a natural leader.","o":[{"t":"Prepare well, pray, and tell God it's His business.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like Brother Lawrence on the barrel boat."},{"t":"Panic and worry all week.","f":"Be careful for nothing; pray instead."},{"t":"Refuse the job.","f":"God can help you do what you can't do alone."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"monkkitchen","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of The Practice of the Presence of God in real life."},{"sc":"home","n":"🍳 Turn chores into time with God."},{"sc":"house","n":"👂 Busy hands, listening heart."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","n":"🥞 Do small things with great love."},{"sc":"barrelboat","n":"🛢️ Hand hard tasks to God: it's His business."}],"stops":{"pg2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"monkkitchen","n":"In the monastery, Brother Lawrence was given a job: cook for the whole community. Every day, he had to feed many hungry monks."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"worried","t":"I'll tell you a secret. I had a great {aversion} to kitchen work. I really didn't like it at all."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgikenna","e":"frown","t":"Same! I hate washing the dishes. It's boring and gross and takes forever."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"So I decided to do it for the love of God. Before I began, I'd say, 'Lord, this is for You. Help me.' And while I worked, I talked with Him, like a friend standing beside me."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","n":"He worked in that kitchen for about fifteen years. And the job he once disliked became one of the happiest places in his life."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"In the noise and clatter of my kitchen, with several people calling for different things at the same time, I have God as peacefully as if I were on my knees in church."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgikenna","e":"worried","t":"So... I could talk to God while I'm washing up?"},{"sc":"home","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Try it, Ikenna! The sink can be a holy place too."},{"sc":"home","n":"Ikenna tried. He thanked God for the food they'd eaten, prayed for each person in his family as he washed their plate, and hummed a worship song. The dishes were done before he knew it."}],"quote":{"text":"The time of business does not with me differ from the time of prayer; and in the noise and clatter of my kitchen... I possess God in as great tranquillity as if I were upon my knees.","who":"The Fourth Conversation","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"The sink can be holy","text":"Brother Lawrence disliked kitchen work, but he did it for the love of God, talking with Him as he worked. For him, work time and prayer time became the same. Your chores can be a place to meet God too."},"think":"Which chore do you dislike most? How could you turn it into time with God this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What job was Brother Lawrence given?","o":["Cook for the monastery","Head monk","Gardener","Bell ringer"],"why":"Feeding many hungry monks."},{"q":"How did he feel about kitchen work at first?","o":["He had a great aversion to it","He loved it","He had never heard of it","He was the best cook ever"],"why":"He really didn't like it."},{"q":"What did he do to change that?","o":["Did it for the love of God and talked with Him while working","Refused to cook","Asked for another job","Cooked badly"],"why":"Lord, this is for You."},{"q":"How did he say he had God in the noisy kitchen?","o":["As peacefully as if on his knees in church","Not at all","Only after work","Only on Sundays"],"why":"Work time and prayer time became the same."},{"q":"What did Ikenna do while washing dishes?","o":["Thanked God and prayed for his family","Complained loudly","Broke the plates","Ran away"],"why":"The dishes were done before he knew it."}]},"pg2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"house","n":"Long before Brother Lawrence, Jesus visited the home of two sisters, Martha and Mary, in the village of Bethany."},{"sc":"house","n":"Martha rushed about, cooking and serving and getting everything ready. Mary sat at Jesus' feet, listening to Him."},{"sc":"house","w":"pgmartha","e":"frown","t":"Lord, dost thou not care that my sister hath left me to serve alone? bid her therefore that she help me."},{"sc":"house","w":"pgjesus","e":"smile","t":"Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things: But one thing is needful: and Mary hath chosen that good part, which shall not be taken away from her."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Now, Jesus wasn't saying cooking is bad! Someone has to cook. But Martha was so busy and worried that she forgot the most important thing: being with Jesus."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"My secret was to be Martha with my hands and Mary with my heart. My hands were busy with pots. My heart was sitting at Jesus' feet."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"smile","t":"So I can have busy hands and a listening heart at the same time!"}],"quote":{"text":"Martha, Martha, thou art careful and troubled about many things: But one thing is needful.","who":"Luke 10:41-42","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Busy hands, listening heart","text":"Martha was so busy serving that she forgot to be with Jesus. Mary sat at His feet. Brother Lawrence learned to be both: Martha with his hands, Mary with his heart. You can do your work and stay close to Jesus at the same time."},"think":"When are you most like Martha, busy and worried? How could you keep a 'Mary heart' at those times?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Martha and Mary live?","o":["Bethany","Rome","Paris","Babylon"],"why":"Jesus visited their home."},{"q":"What was Martha doing?","o":["Rushing about cooking and serving","Sitting at Jesus' feet","Sleeping","Fishing"],"why":"And worrying."},{"q":"What was Mary doing?","o":["Sitting at Jesus' feet, listening","Cooking","Shopping","Cleaning"],"why":"She chose the good part."},{"q":"What did Jesus say Martha was troubled about?","o":["Many things","Nothing","Money","The weather"],"why":"But one thing is needful."},{"q":"What was Brother Lawrence's secret?","o":["Martha with his hands, Mary with his heart","Never cooking","Only praying","Only working"],"why":"Busy hands, listening heart."}]},"pg2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"People think they need to do huge, important things for God. Preach to thousands. Go to faraway lands. But I turned pancakes in the pan, for the love of God!"},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"pgbisola","e":"smirk","t":"Pancakes? For God? Does He really care about pancakes?"},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"He cares about the love you put into them! God doesn't look at how big the job is. He looks at the love behind it."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"When I couldn't do anything else, I would pick up a straw from the ground for the love of God. Small things, done with great love."},{"sc":"home","n":"That evening, Bisola had to fold the family's laundry. Instead of rushing it, she folded each piece neatly, praying for whoever would wear it."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgbisola","e":"smile","t":"Lord, bless Daddy at work tomorrow... Help my little brother in his test... Thank You for Mummy..."},{"sc":"home","n":"It was still just laundry. But now it was laundry done for God."}],"quote":{"text":"We ought not to be weary of doing little things for the love of God, who regards not the greatness of the work, but the love with which it is performed.","who":"The Fourth Conversation","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Small things, great love","text":"Brother Lawrence turned pancakes and picked up straws for the love of God. God doesn't measure how big the job is. He looks at the love behind it. Your smallest task, done with love, is a gift to Him."},"think":"What small thing could you do tomorrow, quietly, just for the love of God?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence turn in the pan for the love of God?","o":["Pancakes","Coins","Books","Stones"],"why":"Small things, great love."},{"q":"What does God look at, according to Brother Lawrence?","o":["The love behind the work","How big the job is","How famous you are","How fast you are"],"why":"Not the greatness of the work."},{"q":"What did he pick up when he couldn't do anything else?","o":["A straw from the ground","A sword","A crown","A bag of gold"],"why":"For the love of God."},{"q":"What did Bisola do while folding laundry?","o":["Prayed for whoever would wear each piece","Complained","Threw it on the floor","Watched TV"],"why":"Laundry done for God."},{"q":"According to 1 Corinthians 10:31, what should we do all things for?","o":["The glory of God","Our own glory","Money","Fun only"],"why":"Even eating and drinking."}]},"pg2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"One day, the monastery sent Brother Lawrence on a long trip to {Burgundy}, to buy the monks' supply of wine for the year."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"worried","t":"Oh dear. I have no head for business at all! And with my bad leg, I can hardly get around a boat."},{"sc":"barrelboat","n":"On the river boat, he couldn't walk easily between the big barrels. So he rolled himself over them to get from one place to another!"},{"sc":"barrelboat","w":"pgikenna","e":"big","t":"Ha! He rolled over the barrels?"},{"sc":"barrelboat","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I did! But I didn't worry about it. I said to God: 'Lord, this is Your business. I'm doing it for You.' And I left it in His hands."},{"sc":"barrelboat","n":"Brother Lawrence told de Beaufort that the whole job went very well. A task he was terrible at turned out fine, because he trusted God with it."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"worried","t":"I have to give a speech next week, and I'm terrible at speeches."},{"sc":"barrelboat","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"Then prepare as well as you can, and tell God: 'This is Your business.' Then stop worrying, and trust Him."}],"quote":{"text":"Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.","who":"Philippians 4:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"It's God's business","text":"Sent to buy wine for the monastery, Brother Lawrence had no head for business and could barely get around the boat. But he told God, 'This is Your business,' and it went well. When you face a task you're bad at, prepare, pray, and trust God with it."},"think":"What task are you dreading? How could you hand it to God as 'His business'?","quiz":[{"q":"Where was Brother Lawrence sent?","o":["To Burgundy","To Rome","To Lagos","To London"],"why":"To buy the monks' supply of wine."},{"q":"Why was it hard for him?","o":["He had no head for business and a bad leg","He was too young","He couldn't swim","He was too rich"],"why":"He could hardly get around a boat."},{"q":"How did he move around the boat?","o":["He rolled himself over the barrels","He flew","He swam","He stood still"],"why":"Ha!"},{"q":"What did he say to God?","o":["'This is Your business'","'I quit'","'Do it for me while I sleep'","Nothing"],"why":"He trusted God with it."},{"q":"According to Philippians 4:6, what should we do instead of worrying?","o":["Pray with thanksgiving","Worry more","Give up","Hide"],"why":"Be careful for nothing."}]}}},"pg3":{"challenge":[{"q":"How did Brother Lawrence react to his failures?","o":["Told God honestly and carried on","Felt terrible for weeks","Hid","Gave up on God"],"why":"No big fuss."},{"q":"Psalm 103:12: as far as the east is from the...","o":["west","north","south","sea"],"why":"So far He removes our sins."},{"q":"What did Coach Musa say champions do?","o":["Get back up","Never fail","Quit early","Blame the ref"],"why":"Everyone misses sometimes."},{"q":"Brother Lawrence wrote that God knows best what is...?","o":["needful for us","fun for us","expensive","easy"],"why":"All He does is for our good."},{"q":"\"Casting all your care upon him; for he...\"","o":["careth for you","is busy","is far away","is asleep"],"why":"1 Peter 5:7."},{"q":"What did Bisola give to God?","o":["Her 'what ifs'","Her phone","Her lunch","Her shoes"],"why":"And God went before her."},{"q":"What did Ikenna compare his wandering mind to?","o":["A puppy that won't sit still","A cat","A bird","A fish"],"why":"Bring it back gently."},{"q":"Isaiah 26:3: God keeps in perfect peace those whose mind is...?","o":["stayed on Him","very busy","empty","clever"],"why":"Because they trust Him."},{"q":"\"There is no fear in...\"","o":["love","night","school","football"],"why":"1 John 4:18."},{"q":"Brother Lawrence did everything for the pure ___ of God.","o":["love","fear","reward","money"],"why":"Not fear, but love."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does 'Haƙuri maganin duniya' mean?","o":["Patience is the medicine of the world","Hurry up","Eat well","Sleep early"],"why":"A Hausa proverb."},"choices":[{"title":"Replaying it","q":"You said something unkind to a friend yesterday and can't stop feeling awful.","o":[{"t":"Say sorry to God and your friend, then carry on with God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Own it, then carry on. No big fuss."},{"t":"Keep beating yourself up for weeks.","f":"That doesn't fix anything. Receive forgiveness."},{"t":"Pretend it never happened.","f":"Be honest, then move on."}]},{"title":"What if?","q":"You're starting at a new club next week and you're full of 'what ifs'.","o":[{"t":"Give each worry to God, and trust Him to go before you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God knows best what is good for you."},{"t":"Stay home so nothing can go wrong.","f":"God is already there."},{"t":"Worry every night until it starts.","f":"Cast all your care on Him."}]},{"title":"Distracted prayer","q":"Your mind keeps wandering when you pray, so you think about giving up.","o":[{"t":"Keep bringing your mind back gently to God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Every return is a 'yes' to God."},{"t":"Give up praying.","f":"Everyone's mind wanders. Keep practising."},{"t":"Get angry with yourself.","f":"Be patient: patience is the medicine of the world."}]},{"title":"Why obey?","q":"Your friend says, \"I only go to church so I don't get in trouble.\"","o":[{"t":"Share that God loves us first, so we can follow Him out of love.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Perfect love casts out fear."},{"t":"Agree. Fear is the main reason.","f":"God wants love, not just fear."},{"t":"Laugh at your friend.","f":"Be kind, and point to God's love."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"racetrack","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of The Practice of the Presence of God in real life."},{"sc":"racetrack","n":"🩹 When you fail, own it, give it to God, and carry on."},{"sc":"home","n":"🕊️ Give God your 'what ifs'. He knows best."},{"sc":"church","n":"🧭 When your mind wanders, come back gently."},{"sc":"home","n":"❤️ Obey God out of love, not fear."}],"stops":{"pg3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"racetrack","n":"Ikenna missed an easy goal in the school football final. His team lost. He couldn't stop thinking about it for days."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"pgikenna","e":"frown","t":"I'm useless. I let everybody down. I keep replaying it in my head."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna, I failed often too. I would lose my temper, or forget God for hours. Do you know what I did?"},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I simply said to God: 'I'll never do any better if You leave me to myself. It's You who must stop me falling, and fix what is wrong.' Then I got up and carried on, with Him."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"pgikenna","e":"shock","t":"That's it? No feeling terrible for weeks?"},{"sc":"monkkitchen","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"Feeling terrible for weeks doesn't fix anything! Be honest with God, say sorry when you've done wrong, receive His forgiveness, and move on. As far as the east is from the west, that's how far He removes our sins."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"pgcoach","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna! Practice tomorrow. Everyone misses sometimes. Champions are the ones who get back up."},{"sc":"racetrack","w":"pgikenna","e":"smile","t":"Okay. I'm getting back up."}],"quote":{"text":"I shall never do otherwise, if You leave me to myself; it is You who must hinder my falling, and mend what is amiss.","who":"The Second Conversation","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Own it, then carry on","text":"When Brother Lawrence failed, he didn't make a big fuss or beat himself up for weeks. He told God honestly, asked Him to help, and carried on. God removes our sins as far as the east is from the west. Get back up!"},"think":"Is there a failure you keep replaying in your head? How could you hand it to God and carry on?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Ikenna miss?","o":["An easy goal in the final","The bus","His homework","Dinner"],"why":"And his team lost."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence do when he failed?","o":["Told God honestly, asked for help, and carried on","Felt terrible for weeks","Hid from God","Gave up"],"why":"No big fuss."},{"q":"Who did Brother Lawrence say must stop him falling?","o":["God","Himself alone","His friends","Nobody"],"why":"'It is You who must hinder my falling.'"},{"q":"How far does God remove our sins?","o":["As far as the east is from the west","A little way","Not at all","Only to next door"],"why":"Psalm 103:12."},{"q":"What did Coach Musa say champions do?","o":["Get back up","Never miss","Quit","Blame others"],"why":"Everyone misses sometimes."}]},"pg3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Bisola's family was moving to a new city. New house, new school, no friends. She lay awake at night, {anxious} and afraid."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgbisola","e":"worried","t":"What if nobody likes me? What if the school is horrible? What if, what if, what if..."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Bisola, in one of my letters I wrote this: God knows best what is good for us, and everything He does is for our good."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I'm not saying you won't feel nervous. But you can tell God every 'what if', and then remember: He's already in that new city. He's already at that new school."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgbisola","e":"worried","t":"Lord, here are all my 'what ifs'. I'm giving them to You. Please go before me."},{"sc":"home","n":"The first week was hard. But on the third day, a girl called Ngozi sat next to her at lunch, and they became firm friends."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgbisola","e":"big","t":"God was already there, waiting for me."}],"quote":{"text":"God knows best what is needful for us, and all that He does is for our good.","who":"From his Letters","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Give God your 'what ifs'","text":"Bisola was full of worries about moving. Brother Lawrence wrote that God knows best and does everything for our good. Tell God every worry, and remember He's already there in your future, waiting for you."},"think":"Write down your biggest 'what if'. Now give it to God in prayer. What does it feel like to let go of it?","quiz":[{"q":"Why was Bisola anxious?","o":["Her family was moving to a new city","She lost her phone","She had a cold","She failed a test"],"why":"New house, new school, no friends."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence write about God?","o":["God knows best what is good for us","God doesn't care","God is too busy","God forgets"],"why":"All He does is for our good."},{"q":"What did Bisola give to God?","o":["All her 'what ifs'","Her shoes","Her bag","Nothing"],"why":"Please go before me."},{"q":"Who sat next to Bisola on the third day?","o":["A girl called Ngozi","Brother Lawrence","Her teacher","Nobody"],"why":"They became firm friends."},{"q":"According to 1 Peter 5:7, why can we cast our cares on God?","o":["Because He cares for us","Because He's bored","Because we must","Because it's Sunday"],"why":"He careth for you."}]},"pg3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"Ikenna tried to pray before bed. He closed his eyes. 'Dear God, thank You for...' Then he started thinking about football. Then about a video he'd watched. Then about lunch tomorrow."},{"sc":"church","w":"pgikenna","e":"frown","t":"I'm hopeless at praying! My mind wanders everywhere!"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Ha! Mine too. In my letters I admitted that the mind is very roving."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"pgikenna","e":"smirk","t":"Like a puppy that won't sit still!"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"When you notice it's wandered, don't get angry with yourself. Just bring it back gently to God, calmly and quietly. And again. And again. That is the practice."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"Every time you bring your mind back, you're choosing God. That's not failing at prayer. That IS prayer."},{"sc":"church","w":"pgikenna","e":"smile","t":"Okay... Dear God, thank You for... oops, football again. Sorry. Back to You, Lord. Thank You for my family..."},{"sc":"church","n":"It took patience. But over the weeks, his mind wandered a little less, and coming back to God got a little easier."}],"quote":{"text":"Thou wilt keep him in perfect peace, whose mind is stayed on thee: because he trusteth in thee.","who":"Isaiah 26:3","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Every return is a 'yes' to God","text":"Ikenna's mind wandered when he prayed. Brother Lawrence said everyone's mind roves. Don't get angry: just bring it back gently to God, again and again. Each time you come back, you're choosing God. That is prayer."},"think":"Next time your mind wanders in prayer, try gently saying 'Back to You, Lord.' How does it feel?","proverb":{"text":"Haƙuri maganin duniya.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Patience is the medicine of the world. Be patient with yourself as you learn to pray."},"quiz":[{"q":"What happened when Ikenna tried to pray?","o":["His mind wandered everywhere","He fell asleep immediately","He sang loudly","Nothing"],"why":"Football, videos, lunch..."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence call the mind in his letters?","o":["Very roving","Always still","Perfect","Asleep"],"why":"It wanders off, like a puppy!"},{"q":"What should you do when your mind wanders?","o":["Bring it back gently to God","Get angry with yourself","Give up praying","Shout"],"why":"Again and again."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence say each return to God is?","o":["Prayer itself: choosing God","Failure","A waste of time","Cheating"],"why":"That IS prayer."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb call patience?","o":["The medicine of the world","A waste of time","Weakness","A punishment"],"why":"Haƙuri maganin duniya."}]},"pg3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"home","w":"pgikenna","e":"worried","t":"Sometimes I only obey God because I'm scared He'll punish me."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I understand, Ikenna. Remember, for years I was full of fear. But I learned to serve God for a different reason."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"I decided to do everything for the pure love of God, not because I was afraid of punishment, and not to win a reward. Just because I love Him, and He loves me."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgmum","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna, why do you help me carry the shopping?"},{"sc":"home","w":"pgikenna","e":"smile","t":"Because I love you, Mum! Not because you'd punish me."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgmum","e":"big","t":"Exactly. That's how God wants us to obey Him too: out of love."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"The Bible says there is no fear in love: perfect love casts out fear. When you know how much God loves you, the fear melts away, and love takes its place."}],"quote":{"text":"We love him, because he first loved us.","who":"1 John 4:19","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Obey out of love","text":"Brother Lawrence once served God out of fear. Then he learned to do everything for the pure love of God. Like helping your mum because you love her, God wants us to obey Him out of love. Perfect love casts out fear."},"think":"Do you obey God more out of fear or out of love? How could knowing His love change that?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Ikenna sometimes obey God?","o":["Because he was scared of punishment","Because he loved Him","Because his friends did","He never did"],"why":"Out of fear."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence decide to do everything for?","o":["The pure love of God","A reward","Fear of punishment","Fame"],"why":"Because he loves God and God loves him."},{"q":"Why did Ikenna help his mum with shopping?","o":["Because he loved her","Because she'd punish him","For money","He didn't"],"why":"Out of love."},{"q":"What casts out fear, according to 1 John 4:18?","o":["Perfect love","Hard work","Money","Strength"],"why":"There is no fear in love."},{"q":"According to 1 John 4:19, why do we love God?","o":["Because He first loved us","Because we must","Because we're scared","Because it's easy"],"why":"His love comes first."}]}}},"pg4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who was Brother Lawrence's letter about short prayers written for?","o":["A soldier","A king","A child","A banker"],"why":"Even on the march."},{"q":"What did he say is enough?","o":["A little lifting up of the heart","A long sermon","A big gift","Nothing"],"why":"However short."},{"q":"\"I have set the LORD always before ___.\"","o":["me","them","Sunday","dinner"],"why":"Psalm 16:8."},{"q":"Where did Elijah hear God?","o":["In a still small voice","In the wind","In the earthquake","In the fire"],"why":"1 Kings 19:12."},{"q":"Acts 17:28: in Him we live, and move, and have our...","o":["being","dinner","money","house"],"why":"He is not far from us."},{"q":"Why is it called the 'practice' of the presence of God?","o":["It becomes a habit by doing it again and again","It's a sport","It's only for monks","It's easy at once"],"why":"Like learning to ride a bike."},{"q":"\"I will bless the LORD at all...\"","o":["times","weekends","parties","costs"],"why":"Psalm 34:1."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence mend in his old age?","o":["Sandals","Clocks","Boats","Roofs"],"why":"For the love of God."},{"q":"In what year did Brother Lawrence die?","o":["1691","1614","1640","1700"],"why":"Aged about seventy-seven."},{"q":"\"Surely goodness and ___ shall follow me.\"","o":["mercy","money","danger","friends"],"why":"Psalm 23:6."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What does the Igbo proverb say is the way to lick hot soup?","o":["Slowly, slowly","Very fast","With a fork","Not at all"],"why":"Habits grow little by little."},"choices":[{"title":"No time to pray","q":"Your day is packed: school, lessons, chores. You say you have no time to pray.","o":[{"t":"Use one-second prayers throughout the day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! A little lifting up of the heart is enough."},{"t":"Skip prayer until the holidays.","f":"Short prayers fit into any day."},{"t":"Feel guilty but do nothing.","f":"Just lift your heart to God, even for a second."}]},{"title":"God feels far","q":"You feel like God is far away and doesn't notice you.","o":[{"t":"Sit quietly and remember: He is nearer than you think.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God is in the still small voice."},{"t":"Wait for something dramatic to prove He's there.","f":"He's often in the quiet, not the earthquake."},{"t":"Decide He doesn't care.","f":"In Him we live, and move, and have our being."}]},{"title":"Forgot again","q":"You meant to remember God all day, but forgot by breakfast.","o":[{"t":"Set a few simple reminders and keep practising.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! It becomes a habit little by little."},{"t":"Give up. It's too hard.","f":"Slowly, slowly is how you lick hot soup."},{"t":"Get angry with yourself.","f":"Be patient. That's why it's called a practice."}]},{"title":"A boring job","q":"You've been given the most boring job in the school play: moving chairs backstage.","o":[{"t":"Do it well, for the love of God, and talk with Him as you work.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Pots or sandals or chairs, it's all for Him."},{"t":"Do it badly. It's not important.","f":"God looks at the love behind the work."},{"t":"Complain to everyone.","f":"Turn it into time with God instead."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use The Practice of the Presence of God in real life."},{"sc":"college","n":"💭 Lift up your heart to God, even for a second."},{"sc":"cave","n":"🌬️ God is nearer than you think."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"🔁 Practise His presence until it becomes a habit."},{"sc":"woodshop","n":"🕯️ Pots, sandals, homework: do it all with God."}],"stops":{"pg4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"Brother Lawrence once wrote a letter about a soldier, a man living in the middle of danger and noise, with no quiet room to pray in."},{"sc":"battle","w":"pgsoldier","e":"worried","t":"How can a soldier pray? We're always marching, always busy, always in danger."},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I remember those days myself! Here is what I wrote: a little lifting up of the heart is enough. One quick thought of God, one act of {inward worship}, even while marching with a sword in your hand. God accepts prayers like that, however short."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"shock","t":"So a prayer can be one second long?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"Yes! 'Lord, help me.' 'Thank You, Father.' 'I love You, Jesus.' Lift your heart to Him in the middle of anything."},{"sc":"college","n":"That week, Bisola tried it. Before her maths test: 'Lord, help me stay calm.' Walking past a beggar: 'Father, please provide for him.' Watching the sunset: 'Thank You, God. It's beautiful.'"},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"big","t":"I prayed more this week than ever before, and I never once had to stop what I was doing!"}],"quote":{"text":"A little lifting up of the heart suffices; a little remembrance of God, one act of inward worship, though upon a march, and sword in hand, are prayers which, however short, are nevertheless acceptable to God.","who":"From his Letters","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Prayers can be short","text":"Brother Lawrence wrote that even a soldier on the march can pray: a little lifting up of the heart is enough. 'Lord, help me.' 'Thank You, Father.' Short prayers in the middle of anything are welcome to God."},"think":"Try five one-second prayers tomorrow: at breakfast, in class, at lunch, on the way home, and before bed.","quiz":[{"q":"Who did Brother Lawrence write about in this letter?","o":["A soldier","A king","A cook","A sailor"],"why":"Living in danger and noise."},{"q":"What did he say is enough?","o":["A little lifting up of the heart","Three hours of prayer","A long speech","Nothing"],"why":"Even on the march."},{"q":"Does God accept very short prayers?","o":["Yes, however short","No, only long ones","Only in church","Only written ones"],"why":"One act of inward worship."},{"q":"What did Bisola pray walking past a beggar?","o":["'Father, please provide for him'","Nothing","'Go away'","'Help me get rich'"],"why":"A one-second prayer."},{"q":"According to Psalm 16:8, where is the LORD?","o":["At my right hand","Far away","Only in heaven","Asleep"],"why":"I shall not be moved."}]},"pg4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"cave","n":"Long ago, the prophet Elijah was exhausted and afraid. He hid in a cave on a mountain. God told him to go out and stand before Him."},{"sc":"mountain","n":"A great, strong wind tore at the mountains and broke the rocks into pieces. But the LORD was not in the wind."},{"sc":"cave","n":"After the wind, an earthquake. But the LORD was not in the earthquake. After the earthquake, a fire. But the LORD was not in the fire."},{"sc":"cave","n":"And after the fire, a still small voice."},{"sc":"cave","n":"When Elijah heard it, he wrapped his face in his cloak, went out, and stood at the entrance of the cave. God was there, in the quiet."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"We often look for God in huge, loud, exciting moments. And sometimes He is there! But mostly He's in the quiet. He's nearer than you think: closer than your breath."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"You don't have to shout to Him from far away. He's right here, inside you and beside you. Just speak to Him quietly, like a friend in the same room."},{"sc":"home","w":"pgikenna","e":"smile","t":"So God isn't far away up in the sky somewhere. He's right here, in my bedroom, now."}],"quote":{"text":"That they should seek the Lord... though he be not far from every one of us: For in him we live, and move, and have our being.","who":"Acts 17:27-28","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God is close","text":"God wasn't in the wind, the earthquake or the fire, but in a still small voice. Brother Lawrence taught that God is nearer than we think. You don't have to shout from far away. Speak to Him quietly, like a friend in the same room."},"think":"Find a quiet moment today. Sit still for one minute and simply remember: God is right here with me.","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Elijah hide?","o":["In a cave","In a boat","In a palace","In a kitchen"],"why":"Exhausted and afraid."},{"q":"Was the LORD in the great wind?","o":["No","Yes","Only a little","The Bible doesn't say"],"why":"Nor in the earthquake or fire."},{"q":"What came after the fire?","o":["A still small voice","A flood","A storm","An army"],"why":"1 Kings 19:12."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence say about how near God is?","o":["He's nearer than you think","He's very far away","He only visits on Sundays","He's too busy"],"why":"Closer than your breath."},{"q":"According to Acts 17:28, in Him we...?","o":["Live, and move, and have our being","Sleep and eat","Work and play","Fight and win"],"why":"He is not far from every one of us."}]},"pg4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"pgikenna","e":"worried","t":"I tried to remember God all day yesterday, but I forgot by 9 o'clock. This is hard!"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Of course it's hard at first! That's why it's called a 'practice'. Like learning a musical instrument or a sport."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"I told Father de Beaufort that at the beginning, you must work at it with care. But after a while, God's love inside you starts to pull you back to Him without any struggle at all."},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"smile","t":"Like learning to ride a bike. At first you wobble and fall. Then one day you just... ride."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"Exactly! Start small. Pick a few moments each day to turn to God: when you wake up, before meals, between lessons, before sleep. Little by little, it becomes the most natural thing in the world."},{"sc":"college","n":"Ikenna set three reminders: breakfast, break time, and bedtime. After a month, he noticed he was talking to God at other times too, without even trying."}],"quote":{"text":"In order to form a habit of conversing with God continually... we must at first apply to Him with some diligence: but after a little care we should find His love inwardly excite us to it without any difficulty.","who":"The First Conversation","tag":"From the Conversations"},"lesson":{"title":"Practice makes a habit","text":"Talking with God all day is hard at first. Brother Lawrence said you must work at it carefully in the beginning, but soon God's love pulls you to Him naturally. Start with a few set moments each day, and let the habit grow."},"think":"Choose three moments in your day to turn to God. Set reminders if it helps. Try it for a month!","proverb":{"text":"Nwayọọ nwayọọ ka e ji aracha ofe dị ọkụ.","lang":"Igbo","mean":"Slowly, slowly is how you lick hot soup. Good habits are built little by little, with patience."},"quiz":[{"q":"When did Ikenna forget about God yesterday?","o":["By 9 o'clock","Never","At midnight","At lunch"],"why":"It's hard at first!"},{"q":"Why is it called a 'practice'?","o":["Because you get better by doing it again and again","Because it's easy","Because it's a game","Because it's only for monks"],"why":"Like learning an instrument."},{"q":"What happens after a while, according to Brother Lawrence?","o":["God's love pulls you to Him without struggle","You get tired","You stop needing God","Nothing"],"why":"It becomes natural."},{"q":"What did Bisola compare it to?","o":["Learning to ride a bike","Eating ice cream","Sleeping","Watching TV"],"why":"Wobble, then ride."},{"q":"What does the Igbo proverb say about hot soup?","o":["Slowly, slowly is how you lick it","Gulp it fast","Throw it away","Let it go cold"],"why":"Little by little."}]},"pg4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"woodshop","n":"As Brother Lawrence grew old, his bad leg made kitchen work too hard. So he was given a new job: mending the monks' {sandals}."},{"sc":"woodshop","w":"lawrence","e":"smile","t":"Pots or sandals, it makes no difference to me. I mend each sandal for the love of God, just as I cooked each meal."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"In his last years he was often ill and in pain. But visitors noticed the same deep peace and joy he'd had for decades. He kept writing letters to encourage his friends to stay close to God."},{"sc":"sickroom","n":"It is recorded that near the end, someone asked him what he was doing. He answered that he was doing what he would do for all eternity: blessing God, praising Him, adoring Him, and loving Him with all his heart."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"Brother Lawrence died peacefully on 12 February 1691, aged about seventy-seven. He had spent more than fifty years in that monastery, mostly in a kitchen and a workshop."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"beaufort","e":"smile","t":"He was never famous in his life. But he had found the greatest treasure of all: the presence of God, every moment of every day."},{"sc":"college","w":"lawrence","e":"big","t":"So, my young friends: talk with God at the sink, at your desk and on the football pitch. When you fail, come back to Him. Lift up your heart, even for a second. He's always with you!"},{"sc":"college","w":"pgbisola","e":"big","t":"Thank you, Brother Lawrence. God at the sink, God at my desk, God everywhere!"},{"sc":"college","w":"pgikenna","e":"big","t":"And God on the football pitch!"}],"quote":{"text":"Surely goodness and mercy shall follow me all the days of my life: and I will dwell in the house of the LORD for ever.","who":"Psalm 23:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"A whole life with God","text":"Brother Lawrence spent his life in a kitchen and a sandal workshop, yet he found the greatest treasure: the presence of God every moment. Even in illness and old age, he was full of peace. You can practise His presence too, starting today."},"think":"Look back over this book. Which idea will you practise first: chores with God, short prayers, coming back gently, or something else?","quiz":[{"q":"What new job did Brother Lawrence get in old age?","o":["Mending the monks' sandals","Ringing bells","Teaching","Gardening"],"why":"His leg made kitchen work too hard."},{"q":"How did he do this new job?","o":["For the love of God, just like cooking","Grumpily","Badly","Only on Sundays"],"why":"Pots or sandals, no difference."},{"q":"What did visitors notice when he was ill?","o":["Deep peace and joy","Anger","Fear","Boredom"],"why":"The same peace he'd had for decades."},{"q":"When did Brother Lawrence die?","o":["1691","1991","1491","1791"],"why":"On 12 February, aged about seventy-seven."},{"q":"What treasure did de Beaufort say he had found?","o":["The presence of God every moment","Gold","Fame","A big house"],"why":"The greatest treasure of all."}]}}}});
